      "classification": "vulnerability",
      "code_path": "beacon-chain/state/state-native/state_trie.go::InitializeFromProtoUnsafeFulu::L649-652",
      "proof_trace": "The invariant is enforced at runtime via SetProposerLookahead (validates length on L18-19), but InitializeFromProtoUnsafeFulu bypasses this check by directly copying the protobuf field without validation (L649-652). States deserialized from SSZ or loaded from the database can have arbitrary proposer lookahead lengths, violating the (MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD+1)*SLOTS_PER_EPOCH invariant.",
      "attack_scenario": "An attacker provides a malicious checkpoint state via SSZ with proposer_lookahead length != 64. The SSZ deserializer (configfork.go:171) or database loader (state.go:552) calls InitializeFromProtoUnsafeFulu, which accepts the invalid length. Subsequent ProcessProposerLookahead calls assume correct length for array indexing (transition.go:34-35), causing out-of-bounds access or incorrect proposer selection.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-56ad1eb2-inv-006"
    },
    "text": "Proposer lookahead length must always be (MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD+1)*SLOTS_PER_EPOCH after epoch processing.",
    "assertion": "forall state s post epoch: len(s.proposer_lookahead) == (MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD+1)*SLOTS_PER_EPOCH",
    "covers": "SG-008",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "type": "invariant"
  }
}

